ote in the  election the ruling AKP is all so  vigorously campaigning on the streets  their candidate for mayor pinellia  Durham was Turkey's Prime Minister until  last year he's playing on his political  experience but president add one who  held one election rally after another in  support of his man in the initial vote  in spring is now noticeably holding back  nevertheless the party's volunteers say  they're sure of victory  the CHP is definitely trying to create  the impression that they've already won  but we're optimistic in the first round  our votes were stolen and now we're  going to get them back  voters keep telling us that they want  Benally used room for mayor and God  willing people win whoever wins Istanbul  wins turkey is a well-known saying  coined by president ad one himself this  time around many voters in this  significant city would be happy of the  winner of the election would also be  recognized as such and we can go to  Yulia she is in Istanbul for Yulia is  there a clear front-runner at this stage  opinion polls here in Turkey are  considered notoriously unreliable but  most of them show the opposition Canada  a creamy mamalu ahead with up to 8  percentage points but I met president ad  on yesterday in a rare meeting with  foreign journalists where he dismissed  these surveys as manipulative and made  on order the real Paul adorn says would  take place on Sunday so despite the  opposition and a crummy mama Lu being  hopeful that they can win again there is  a lot of uncertainty as to what will  happen on Election Day now Julia you  joined Ekrem Imam Aloha on the campaign  trail who is he what can you tell us  about him well until a few months ago he  was little known even here in Turkey he  was the mayor of an outlying district of  Istanbul but the fact that he narrowly  won the election in March and when was  then stripped of his mandate at the  request of the ruling party propelled  him onto the national stage he has led  an all-embracing